IMPORT prelude

-- The Kwong-Wai-Shiu Free Hospital (Transfer of Undertaking and Dissolution) Act 2017 (Singapore, No. 21 of 2017) -- what
-- passes to the successor company (ss 2, 3(1), 5), who answers for claims and judgments (s 3(2)), what the transfer does NOT do
-- to contracts, sureties and leases (s 3(3), (4)), registration of the transfer (s 3(5)), trustees and committee members
-- ceasing without compensation (s 4), and the Minister's determination of disputes (s 6).
--
-- Edition: informal consolidation, "version in force from 2/7/2017", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/TKWSFHTUDA2017.txt (retrieved 1 October 2026, "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026"). The
-- deposit shows no amendment annotations.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0261 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. The people it touches are the hospital's creditors, debtors, counterparties, lessees,
-- litigants, trustees and committee members.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: commencement and the transfer date (s 1, s 2 "transfer date" -- both fixed by Gazette notification, and neither
-- date is in the deposit); the employees (s 7 only preserves s 18A of the Employment Act, which is not encoded here); the
-- dissolution and repeal of the Ordinance (s 8) beyond their mention; the saving of others' rights (s 9); and the Income Tax Act
-- amendment (s 10), whose deleted item the deposit does not reproduce.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `The Kwong-Wai-Shiu Free Hospital (Transfer of Undertaking and Dissolution) Act 2017`

DECLARE `Kind of property` IS ONE OF
    `land or an interest in land`
    `money or securities`
    `a chose in action`
    `plant or equipment`
    `intellectual property`
    `a licence or permit`
    `records`

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    `the transferor`
    `the successor company`
    `not decided by this Act`

§§ `2, 3(1) and 5 -- what passes`

-- s 2 "asset": "property of any kind of the transferor IN SINGAPORE on the eve of the transfer date", including (a) interests in
-- real or personal property "situated in Singapore", (b) choses in action, (c) money or securities, (d) plant or equipment
-- "situated in Singapore", (e) intellectual property, (f) infrastructure "situated in Singapore", (g) records, (h) rights --
-- which include "any licence, certificate or permit under any written law".
-- s 2 "liability": "any liability, duty or obligation of the transferor on the eve of the transfer date (whether actual or
-- contingent, liquidated or unliquidated ...)". No "in Singapore" limit.
-- s 3(1): "On the transfer date, all assets and liabilities of the transferor are transferred to the successor company."
-- (2)(a): they vest "without the need for any further conveyance, transfer, assignment or assurance".
-- s 5: "From the transfer date, ALL records of the transferor become the records of the successor company." "records" is
-- defined as records "of the transferor existing on the eve of the transfer date", again with no "in Singapore".
--
-- Reading (an inference, not stated): property outside Singapore is not an "asset" and does not pass under s 3, but records do
-- pass under s 5 wherever they are kept; and liabilities pass wherever they arise.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of property`, `held by the transferor on the eve of the transfer date` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property passes to the successor company` IF
        `held by the transferor on the eve of the transfer date`
    AND (    `in Singapore`
         OR  `the kind` EQUALS `records`)

GIVEN `owed by the transferor on the eve of the transfer date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the liability passes to the successor company` IF
    `owed by the transferor on the eve of the transfer date`

-- s 3(2)(a): no further conveyance or assignment is needed.
GIVEN `the property passes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a further conveyance or assignment is needed` IF
    NOT `the property passes`

§§ `3(2)(b)-(h) -- who answers for claims, proceedings and judgments`

-- (b) the transferred liabilities "become by virtue of this section the liabilities of the successor company";
-- (c) proceedings "started before the transfer date by or against the transferor and pending immediately before that date are
-- taken to be proceedings pending by or against the successor company";
-- (d) proceedings that "could have been started immediately before the transfer date ... may be started by or against the
-- successor company";
-- (e) a judgment or order obtained before the transfer date "may be enforced by or against the successor company";
-- (h) a reference to the transferor in any written law, contract or document, "to the extent to which the reference relates to
-- those assets or liabilities, is taken to be, or to include, a reference to the successor company".
--
-- The Act does not say who answers for a liability that was not the transferor's on the eve of the transfer date; that case
-- returns `not decided by this Act`.
GIVEN `relates to a transferred asset or liability` IS A BOOLEAN, `on or after the transfer date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Party
DECIDE `the party to sue or enforce against` IS
    IF NOT `on or after the transfer date`
    THEN `the transferor`
    ELSE IF `relates to a transferred asset or liability`
         THEN `the successor company`
         ELSE `not decided by this Act`

§§ `3(3) and 3(4) -- what the transfer does not do`

-- s 3(3): "The operation of this section does not -- (a) constitute a breach of, or default under, an Act or other law or
-- otherwise a civil wrong or criminal wrong; (b) constitute a breach of duty of confidence ...; (c) constitute a breach of any
-- contractual provision prohibiting, restricting or regulating the assignment or transfer of assets or liabilities or the
-- disclosure of any information; (d) terminate an agreement or fulfil any condition that allows a person to terminate any
-- agreement ...; (e) cause any contract or instrument to be void or otherwise unenforceable; (f) frustrate any contract;
-- (g) release a surety or other obligor (in whole or part) from an obligation; or (h) constitute an event of breach of, or
-- default under, any contract or other instrument."
-- s 3(4): "No attornment to the successor company by a lessee from the transferor is required."
--
-- These protect against consequences of the transfer itself. A counterparty's rights arising on some other ground are not
-- touched (inference from "The operation of this section does not").
DECLARE `Counterparty response` IS ONE OF
    `terminate the agreement`
    `treat the transfer as a breach of an anti-assignment clause`
    `treat the transfer as a breach of confidence`
    `call an event of default`
    `treat the contract as void or unenforceable`
    `treat the contract as frustrated`
    `claim the guarantor is released`
    `insist the lessee attorn to the successor company`

GIVEN `the response` IS A `Counterparty response`, `grounded only on the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the counterparty may rely on the response` IF
    NOT `grounded only on the transfer`

§§ `3(5) -- registering the transfer`

-- s 3(5): the Registrar of Titles and any other registering authority "must, on the application of the successor company,
-- lodged in registrable form, register or record in the appropriate manner the transfer to the successor company of any of the
-- transferred assets or liabilities".
GIVEN `the successor company applied` IS A BOOLEAN, `lodged in registrable form` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the asset or liability was transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must register the transfer` IF
        `the successor company applied`
    AND `lodged in registrable form`
    AND `the asset or liability was transferred`

§§ `4 -- trustees and committee members`

-- s 4(1): "On the transfer date, every trustee and every committee member stops being a trustee or a committee member".
-- (2): this "does not entitle the trustee or committee member to any payment or other benefit MERELY because he or she stops
-- being such a trustee or committee member".
-- "merely" leaves room for an entitlement on another ground; whether one exists is outside this Act (inference).
GIVEN `appointed before the transfer date` IS A BOOLEAN, `on or after the transfer date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `still holds office as trustee or committee member` IF
        `appointed before the transfer date`
    AND (NOT `on or after the transfer date`)

GIVEN `has an entitlement on some other ground` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the former trustee is entitled to a payment` IF
    `has an entitlement on some other ground`

§§ `6 -- disputes over what was transferred`

-- s 6(1): if a dispute arises "(a) as to whether an asset or a liability or record is transferred under section 3 or 5; or (b) as
-- to whether any, or any part of any, contract or document relates to an asset or a liability or record transferred", "the
-- Minister MAY determine the matter and is to provide the concerned parties with written notice of that determination".
-- (2): "The determination of the Minister under subsection (1) is final and binding on the successor company."
--
-- The Act names only the successor company as bound. Whether the other party to the dispute is bound it does not say; this
-- encoding answers only what the Act makes binding.
DECLARE `Disputant` IS ONE OF
    `the successor company itself`
    `a creditor, debtor or counterparty`

DECLARE `Dispute` IS ONE OF
    `whether an asset, liability or record was transferred`
    `whether a contract or document relates to a transferred item`
    `whether a debt is owed at all`

GIVEN `the dispute` IS A `Dispute`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may determine the dispute` IF
    CONSIDER `the dispute`
    WHEN `whether a debt is owed at all` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the disputant` IS A `Disputant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act makes the determination binding on` IF
    CONSIDER `the disputant`
    WHEN `the successor company itself` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
